Z||000019||California Kid||12-14-2001||12:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GodSend:<BR><B>Hey California Kid - I like the CarbonFiber - Is that the real deal, or the stick on type stuff?  Either way it looks slick.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It's the real stuff, just not compressed, and is covered with a very heavy clear. Very beautiful in the sunlight, as you see a rainbow of colors in the fiber. As it isn't compressed for strength, this stuff has a very thin 3M adhesive on the back side to got over original parts. These parts came from "The Fiero Store".<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picture_010_1.jpg"> <BR>This is the "high pressure" real stuff, very light weight. It still refacts light, but it's not as rich and deep as uncompressed. Parts are on my ZX7R.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picture_073.jpg"> <BR> <P><p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
