Z||000024||watts||12-15-2001||11:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TTiger:<BR><B>WOW, watts has a dash that looks just like mine right now.  I thought mine was custom   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heh...  actually, that was just for a few hours while i saw ripping out my old interior and wiring harness, and replacing it all.  It's looooong since been put back together.  It IS my daily driver.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyhow!  Here's a pic of a Metric 180km/h dash from an '88 Formula.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formuladash.jpg"> <P>Now you can see why it's so easy (more or less) to just screw with the board on the speedo, and have this read as 180MPH.  Just ignore where it says km/h, and ignore the inner ring (which is in MPH).<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
